course: dictionary
lesson: 13577
title: Words that never stop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Incessantly» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. It means without stopping, all the time. Look at the words around it to find its meaning: the clues show what keeps going.
explain: «The baby cried incessantly all night.» Tired parents would not want a crying that stops and starts, and the clue all night tells you the crying went on and on. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in "without stopping" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Writers often use incessantly when something is annoying. «Sam's little brother chatters incessantly about dinosaurs.» Chatters shows talking, and incessantly tells you it goes on so long that it becomes tiresome. Noticing this helps you hear how the writer feels.
fact: Incessantly means without stopping, all the time.
fact: «Incessantly» often shows something annoying that goes on and on.
fact: Phrases to know: «talk incessantly», «rain incessantly», «complain incessantly».
fact: Context clues such as all night or all week show that something has not stopped.
fact: A good check is to swap in "without stopping" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The rain fell incessantly all week.» What does incessantly mean here? | Sometimes, in short bursts | *Without stopping | Very gently, just now and then | Under the umbrella
exercise: Mia's dad says the phone rang incessantly. What does this tell you? | The phone rang once and then went quiet | *The phone kept ringing and never stopped | The phone was broken and silent | The phone was brand new
exercise: «The geese honked incessantly at the gate.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the honking did not stop. | geese | gate | honked | *incessantly
test: «The dog barked incessantly at the postman.» What does barked incessantly show? | The dog was gentle and calm | The dog barked once and then went quiet | The dog was fast asleep | *The dog barked without stopping, all the time
test: Ella says, «Stop talking incessantly!» Why is Ella cross? | Her friend is whispering quietly | Her friend has gone home | *Her friend keeps talking and will not stop | Her friend is singing a song
exam: Which sentence uses incessantly correctly? | Incessantly, the children ate a sandwich at lunch | *The alarm beeped incessantly until someone turned it off | The alarm was incessantly on the wall | The alarm beeped once, softly, at noon
